The headline survives the easiest wrong reading: “agreed to decide” announces review, not approval of detention or a detention count. The first story sentence says what happened. No person is named before introduction. The dek explains the practical old and new positions, but repeats material below. The first paragraph leans on “applicant for admission” and “seeking admission” before showing their difference. **That paragraph fails a cold read.**

