## Holes

1. **What is wrong with the “tens of thousands” reading?** The [question presented](/Volumes/4/GitHub/the-catch-site-wt-detention/data/sources/immigration-detention/scotus-question-presented-2026-10-01.txt) asks whether section 1225 “mandates the detention pending removal proceedings” of this group; the [Fourth Circuit](/Volumes/4/GitHub/the-catch-site-wt-detention/data/sources/immigration-detention/ca4-bond-2026-09-10.txt) reports district courts “sided with the petitioners in over twenty thousand individual cases.” Neither wording supplies a count of people currently detained under this reading. This changes **answer 3** and displaces edit **7** and the competing quantities in edit **8**. The actual detention count remains unknown; the page states that limit.

2. **How can this man have the statutory label without seeking entry?** The [statute](/Volumes/4/GitHub/the-catch-site-wt-detention/data/sources/immigration-detention/uscode-2024-title8-1225.txt) says “An alien present in the United States who has not been admitted” is deemed an applicant for admission. The [Second Circuit](/Volumes/4/GitHub/the-catch-site-wt-detention/data/sources/immigration-detention/ca2-cunha-opinion-2026-04-28.txt) says “Petitioner may be an “applicant for admission,”” and “but he is not “seeking admission.”” This changes **answer 4**. A plain sentence connecting those statements displaces the exceptions in edit **3**; it needs no additional statutory detail.

