data/sources/immigration-detention/doj-petition-26-104.txt-71-(1a) APPENDIX A UNITED STATES COURT OF APPEALS FOR THE SECOND CIRCUIT No. 25-3141-pr August Term 2025 RICARDO APARECIDO BARBOSA DA CUNHA, PETITIONER, APPELLEE v. JOSEPH E. FREDEN, DEPUTY FIELD OFFICE DIRECTOR, U.S. IMMIGRATION AND CUSTOMS ENFORCEMENT, RESPONDENT-APPELLANT*1 Argued: Apr. 6, 2026 Decided: Apr. 28, 2026 Appeal from the United States District Court for the Western District of New York No. 6:25-cv-6532, Meredith A. Vacca, Judge. Before: CABRANES, BIANCO, and NATHAN, Circuit Judges. The government appeals from a grant of a writ of habeas corpus. Petitioner-Appellee Ricardo Aparecido Barbosa da Cunha (“Petitioner”) is a noncitizen from Brazil, who entered the United States without inspection and admission in or around 2005 and has lived in the * The Clerk of Court is respectfully directed to amend the official case caption as set forth above.
